olution", "verb": "FRAMES", "targetSlug": "doctor-zhivago", "targetName": "Doctor Zhivago", "context": "The Cultural Revolution in China echoed the sentiments found in "Doctor Zhivago", emphasizing individual suffering amidst political turmoil."}], "places": [{"name": "Moscow, Russia", "role": "Major setting"}, {"name": "Petrograd, Russia", "role": "Political center during revolution"}, {"name": "Siberia, Russia", "role": "Exile and suffering"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Doctor Zhivago", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "doctor-zhivago"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q206870", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Zhivago_(novel)"], "tags": ["literary work", "Novels & Prose Fiction", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Doctor Zhivago contributed to the historical record of the Modern period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": ""Doctor Zhivago" profoundly impacted perceptions of the Russian Revolution and totalitarianism, influencing literary discourse and political thought across the world. Its ban in the USSR and subsequent Nobel Prize recognition highlighted the clash between art and state, shaping the narrative of artistic freedom in the 20th century.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-11T13:57:41Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27351656017", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "1957 historical novel by boris pasternak Created by Boris Pasternak. Created c. 1945.", "newValue": ""Doctor Zhivago," a historical novel authored by Boris Pasternak, was published in 1957 and has since become a cornerstone of 20th-century literature. Set against the backdrop of the Russian Revolution and World War I, the narrative intricately weaves the personal and the political, depicting how the tumultuous events of the early 20th century shaped individual lives. The novel's exploration of love, loss, and the struggle for identity mirrors the broader societal upheavals in Russia, making it not only a work of fiction but also a poignant commentary on the human condition during a time of crisis. Its significance is further underscored by its controversial reception in the Soviet Union, where Pasternak was denounced for his critical portrayal of the regime.

The novel follows the life of Yuri Zhivago, a physician and poet, as he navigates the chaos of revolution and civil war. Key events include the Bolshevik Revolution of 1917, the subsequent civil war, and the impact of World War I on Russian society. Through Zhivago's relationships, particularly with Lara Antipova, the narrative illustrates the personal struggles faced by individuals caught in the sweep of history. The book was written during the late 1940s and completed in 1955, but its publication was met with significant political backlash, leading to Pasternak's exile from the Soviet literary community.

